Post-Drug Syndromes Research Library
Licensing, by part of this repository

====================================================================
1. The library's own content: CC BY 4.0
====================================================================

The curated content of the library is licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0).

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

This covers the parts of the library that were written or assembled
for it, including:

  * the record summaries, paraphrases, plain-language layers,
    key points and "In the library" notes;
  * the mechanism matrix, its ratings and its evidence notes;
  * the glossary definitions, the timeline entries and their
    significance notes, the topic summaries, the open questions,
    the body-systems review and the pathway maps;
  * the gene reference cards, apart from the third-party reference
    data they cite;
  * the record structure, identifiers, verification statuses,
    cross-links, similarity map and release files
    (releases/*/*.json, *.csv, *.md).

To comply with the license, credit the library, name the release you
used and link to it. The citation formats on
https://postdrugsyndrome.com/research/methodology#cite do this.

====================================================================
2. Quoted and cited source material: not licensed here
====================================================================

The library describes and quotes material it does not own. Copyright
in that material stays with its authors and publishers, and CC BY 4.0
above does not extend to it. This includes:

  * the papers, abstracts, regulatory documents and web pages the
    records point to;
  * short verbatim quotations kept as context, including quoted
    forum and Reddit comments, which are reproduced for research and
    commentary with usernames removed;
  * posts, comments, talks and transcripts by named third parties,
    including Dr Will Powers, which are attributed to them;
  * documents hosted with their author's permission
    (corpus/documents/), which remain their author's;
  * third-party reference data, under its own license as each page
    states: UniProt (CC BY 4.0), Reactome (CC BY 4.0), NCBI Gene,
    PubMed and PubMed Central records.

Reusing any of that is between you and its rights holder.

====================================================================
3. No source code here
====================================================================

This repository holds release files only. The software that builds
the library and runs the site is not included and is not licensed
here.

====================================================================
4. Not medical advice
====================================================================
====================================================================

The library is for research and personal reference. Nothing in it is
a diagnosis, a treatment recommendation or dosing guidance, and the
license above grants no warranty of any kind. Statements by named
clinicians are their own hypotheses. Patient accounts are
uncontrolled self-reports.
